From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Winter <danielwinterw@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:20:16 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] models: expose glm5-next stage graph semantics

The stage planner rejected every GLM-5.3-Flash range: the glm5-next
builder read and wrote its recurrent, MLA and indexer caches without
declaring them, so the delta-net SSM write registered by
build_recurrent_attn landed after unregistered build_rs copies of the
same storage, and the NextN graph left the indexer cache as an
unresolved structural leaf.

Declare the graph semantics the way kimi-linear, qwen3next and
qwen4exp do. The KDA layer reads conv and SSM state through the typed
build_rs, and each rollback slot of the conv window is a registered
recurrent_conv write. The DSA layer registers its MLA latent write and
read, and the indexer cache's key write, pooled-key scatter and read,
as kv_key effects, so the trunk and the NextN head carry explicit
ownership. The k-pool inputs are bound as request inputs.

Tests: a synthetic graph contract at the production trunk depth (45),
width (4096) and one NextN head checks every two-stage cut, a
three-stage chain and the terminal-stage MTP contract. A dense NextN
fixture runs live MTP sync and drafting against an independently
loaded reference; the fixture generator now writes glm5-next's
per-layer KV head counts over the NextN block.
